    "dcterms:description": [
        {
            "@value": "Know your Navy / These two booklets tell you all the facts. Ask for your copies today at the nearest U.S. Navy Recruiting Station / 1. “What Kind of Job Can I Get in the Navy?” This booklet is a guide to the vocational opportunities of the Navy. It describes the Navy’s 50 ratings, giving pay, duties and insignia of each. It tells about the Navy trade schools and how your civilian occupation may qualify you at once for a petty officer rating. / 2. “Men Make the Navy . . . The Navy Makes Men” This booklet tells you all the things you want to know about life in the Navy—requirements for enlistment, pay rates, allowances for dependents, opportunities for promotion, food, medical and dental care, clothing allotment, training routine, recreation, ratings, etc. / Don’t wait—Choose the Navy",
            "is_public": true,
            "property_id": 4,
            "property_label": "Description",
            "type": "literal"
